  "question": {
    "text": "A stationary balloon is observed from three points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> on the plane ground and is found that its angle of elevation from each point is <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8736;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> meters, then the height of the balloon from the ground is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> meters",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> be vertical with height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;meters&nbsp;and at its end <math><mi>Q</mi></math> there is a balloon and <math><mi>P</mi></math> is on the ground<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>cot</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mi>P</mi></math> is the circumcentre of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and its circumradius <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0056_160f8549894b.png\" style=\"width:1.96667in;height:1.71319in\" /><br />In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> meters."
  }
